  - key: lubang
    title:
      id: Lubang di gagang
      en: The finger ring
    text:
      id: 'Perhatikan lubang di ujung gagang. Karambit dipegang dengan jari telunjuk
        masuk ke lubang ini, sehingga bilahnya keluar dari bawah kepalan tangan.
        Karena itu karambit sulit dirampas. Perajin di Sungai Pua, Agam, punya pedoman
        turun-temurun: gagang idealnya selebar empat buku jari. Gagang ini dibuat
        dari kayu kemuning, kayu yang dipercaya bertuah.'
      en: 'Notice the ring at the end of the grip. The karambit is held with the
        index finger through this ring, so the blade comes out from below the fist.
        That makes it hard to take away. The makers of Sungai Pua, in Agam, follow
        a guideline handed down for generations: the grip should ideally be four
        knuckles wide. This grip is made of kemuning wood, believed to carry spiritual
        power.'
    stage: 1
    focusHotspot: lubang
    voiceID: {fileID: 8300000, guid: e1877d97ca628724d95d9102ff322823, type: 3}
    voiceEN: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 0823377be522dd44ebbfa6aae900d88a, type: 3}
